  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🕹️ PSN Name Generator",
      "tagline": "PlayStation online IDs that fit the rules, from Cinder-Lark to PlatChaser."
    },
    "intro": "A PlayStation online ID can use hyphens as well as underscores, which gives it a look most gamertags can't have. This **PSN name generator** makes IDs of 3 to 16 characters in five styles (hyphenated, clan tag, trophy hunter, aesthetic and funny) and can build them around a word or name of your own. It's an unofficial tool, not made by or connected with Sony Interactive Entertainment or PlayStation.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good PSN names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, from every style:</p><ul><li><strong>Cinder-Lark</strong>: two words with a hyphen, a look many platforms don't allow.</li><li><strong>Kite-of-Juniper</strong>: three parts and still only 15 characters.</li><li><strong>RVN-Rook</strong>: a clan tag in front, so the whole squad can share RVN.</li><li><strong>PlatChaser</strong>: for a player who won't put a game down until the Platinum pops.</li><li><strong>HiddenHoarder</strong>: a nod to hidden trophies, the ones the game won't describe until you earn them.</li><li><strong>velvet_static</strong>: aesthetic, soft and all in lower case.</li><li><strong>Couch_Goblin</strong>: funny, and honest about where most gaming happens.</li><li><strong>Cutscene_Skipper</strong>: exactly 16 characters, and everyone knows one.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "PlayStation online ID rules",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Length:</strong> 3 to 16 characters.</li><li><strong>Characters:</strong> letters, numbers, hyphens (-) and underscores (_). No spaces, full stops or symbols, so <em>Couch Goblin</em> becomes <em>Couch_Goblin</em> or <em>Couch-Goblin</em>.</li><li><strong>Changing it:</strong> you can change your online ID as often as you like. The first change is free and later ones cost money, and you can choose to show your old ID next to the new one for 30 days so friends know it's you.</li><li><strong>Child accounts</strong> can't change their online ID.</li><li><strong>Breaking the rules:</strong> if a new ID breaks PlayStation's terms of service, it's replaced with a temporary one (temp- and some characters) until you choose another.</li></ul><p>Every name here fits those rules and starts with a letter, which is the safe choice. If you type your own word, start it with a letter too.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Hyphens, clan tags and trophies",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Hyphenated:</strong> mineral, tree and colour words joined to birds and wanderers (Cinder-Lark, Granite-Kite). A hyphen keeps two words readable without a space.</li><li><strong>Clan tag:</strong> in many games a clan shows its tag in brackets, but brackets aren't allowed in an online ID, so players put the tag in front with a hyphen or underscore: RVN-Rook, KRKN_Moth. The tags here are invented, not real esports teams.</li><li><strong>Trophy hunter:</strong> PlayStation games award Bronze, Silver, Gold and Platinum trophies, and the Platinum usually means you've earned every other trophy in the game. Names like PlatChaser and Gold_Magpie are for players who love the grind.</li><li><strong>Aesthetic:</strong> soft words in lower case, joined with an underscore, a hyphen or nothing at all (velvet_static, softorbit).</li><li><strong>Funny:</strong> sofa-gaming jokes like Couch_Goblin and Button-Masher.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you change",
        "content": "<p>The names here are free to use, but you need to check each one is available. On PlayStation's change online ID page, or in your console's account settings, type the name and check it before you confirm. Since only the first change is free, try a few here first.</p><p>Also on Xbox? The <a href=\"xbox-gamertag-generator.html\">Xbox Gamertag Generator</a> makes tags that fit Xbox's 12 characters, spaces included. If you stream, the <a href=\"twitch-name-generator.html\">Twitch Name Generator</a> follows Twitch's rules, and for a clan to go with your tag, try the <a href=\"clan-name-generator.html\">Clan Name Generator</a>. The <a href=\"gamertag-generator.html\">Gamertag Generator</a> makes names for any platform.</p>"
      }
    ],
